# Corpus unit adaptive-pruning/C03 — gap (T2 exemplar: the unmet-mandatory-CQ path)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/adaptive-pruning.yaml C03 (comparative, controlled_comparison;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: APT matches Prune+Distill (CoFi) accuracy on MNLI/SST2 at 60%
# sparsity on RoBERTa-base within 0.9 points, with 41.6% of its peak training memory and 2.5x
# faster 97% time-to-accuracy (E01 Table 2, steps 4/7; E04 Table 10).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * E01/E04 specify no seeds or repeated runs, so corpus-v1's mandatory variance_reported CQ
#     has no discharging leaf. An argument with an open mandatory obligation is an
#     IncompleteArgument REJECTION (Check.checkArguments), so no complete
#     controlled_comparison(apt, prune_distill_cofi, ...) instance is declarable: the unit is
#     E2-style — the claim and every existing evidence leaf are on the page, no arg binds them,
#     and the claim lands `gap` on empty complete support (M4a decision #8).
#   * Policy-vs-annotation divergence, recorded per the uniform-standard rule: the M0 annotator
#     rated the variance CQ OPTIONAL for this claim ("leaves the tightness of 'within 0.9
#     points' unestablished but does not defeat it"); corpus-v1 makes variance mandatory
#     family-wide (27 mandatory vs 16 optional annotations corpus-wide), and the policy call
#     wins. The would-be argument's other CQs are all annotated met.
#   * Q constant train_cost_at_parity names the claim's real content: training cost (memory,
#     TTA) at matched accuracy. The 0.9-point / 41.6% / 2.5x figures live in `nl` and refs.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact adaptive-pruning at sha256:de3685165a53
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c03
  nl      = "APT achieves accuracy on par with Prune+Distill (CoFi) on MNLI/SST2 at 60% sparsity on RoBERTa-base (within 0.9 points) with 41.6% of its training memory and 2.5x faster 97% TTA"
  formal  = better(apt, prune_distill_cofi, train_cost_at_parity, roberta_mnli_sst2)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E01's comparison cells (MNLI/SST2 accuracy parity, memory ratio, TTA
# speedup) plus E04's self-distillation cost accounting, folded into refs per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(apt, prune_distill_cofi, train_cost_at_parity, roberta_mnli_sst2, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C03, E01#Table-2, E01#steps-4-7, E04#Table-10, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N15]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(apt, prune_distill_cofi, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [E01#Procedure-step-6, E01#Setup]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(train_cost_at_parity, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [E01#Procedure-steps-4-7]

leaf e4 : scope_matched(apt, train_cost_at_parity, roberta_mnli_sst2)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [E01#Baselines]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: variance_reported(e01) has no honest leaf — E01/E04 report single
# runs — and corpus-v1 makes that obligation mandatory. The claim's complete-support set is
# therefore empty.)

status c03

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments.
# Claim status:
#   c03 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8)
